The seasonal pattern confirms that BESS value is concentrated in high-wind months, where curtailment without storage reaches 27--31\%. HQI-SAC-Fed's learned dispatch policy adaptively increases charging aggressiveness during high-wind forecast periods, informed by the GCN embedding that captures network-wide generation and congestion conditions. Summer curtailment is inherently lower (11--13\% baseline) due to reduced wind capacity factors and higher cooling-driven demand, yielding smaller but still meaningful reductions to 3--5\%.

\subsection{Economic Analysis}

Table~\ref{tab:economics} presents the detailed economic breakdown for HQI-SAC-Fed over the 15-year NPV horizon at 5\% discount rate.

